  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A body having specific charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is resting on a frictionless plane at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the wall (as shown in the figure). It starts moving towards the wall when a uniform electric field of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is applied horizontally towards the wall. If the collision of the body with the wall is perfectly elastic, then the time period of the motion will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ded9df93-3660-45d5-90da-9556de6cec90-image.png\" style=\"width: 414px; height: 195px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/db7e52e7-f21e-4dec-94cb-405e138f4f8d-image.png\" style=\"width: 368px; height: 225px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></math><br />Now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Time period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math><br />Answer&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn></math></p>",
